  "semantics": [
    "The prefer-left fold processes every original occurrence. The pinned append-fit theorem proves the untested right-bin bound.",
    "All four public remainder budgets derive every later remaining-square test from full original support and the exact original preceding product.",
    "p2 additionally needs p1^2*p2<=D; p1p3 additionally needs p1*p2^2*p3<=D; p2p3 additionally needs p1^2*p2*p3<=D.",
    "The public allocate wrappers produce literal actualTwoCapacityFactors with product a*b0*c=original.prod, a<=A, c<=D/(A*b0).",
    "Original primality, original Nodup, and the literal product identity supply all three pairwise coprimalities through squarefreeness.",
    "The C<1 repair reruns on the full original vector and may replace b0; it separately needs 1<=D/A."
  ],
  "remaining_gates": [
    "The extra initial square gates are genuine and do not follow from arbitrary full support alone.",
    "Selected remainder allocation explicitly needs 1<=A and 1<=D/(A*b0).",
    "No alpha perturbation, three analytic monomial estimates, fixed whole-box slot partition or same-policy arithmetic mean follows from these two files."
  ],
